{"format":1,"key":"zone:thunderbluff","path":"/lore/zone/thunderbluff","name":"Thunder Bluff","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"thunderbluff","name":"Thunder Bluff","path":"/lore/zone/thunderbluff"},"levels":"","description":"Thunder Bluff is the magnificent capital city of the tauren, perched atop windswept red-rock mesas rising above the grasslands of Mulgore. Founded by…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:thunderbluff","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Thunder Bluff is the magnificent capital city of the tauren, perched atop windswept red-rock mesas rising above the grasslands of Mulgore. Founded by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof after uniting the nomadic tribes with the aid of the New Horde, it serves as the cultural, spiritual, and mercantile heart of his people. Connected by swaying rope bridges and wooden lifts, the city offers safety from centaur marauders and a peaceful sanctuary for travelers across Kalimdor.","For countless generations, the tauren lived as nomadic wanderers across Kalimdor, locked in a brutal struggle for survival against ravenous centaur tribes. That desperate era ended during the Third War when Cairne Bloodhoof joined forces with Warchief Thrall. Together, the orcs and tauren broke the centaur assaults and secured the lush pastures of Mulgore. To protect their future, Cairne led the allied tribes to the safety of these natural stone bastions, founding Thunder Bluff as the first unified, permanent home the tauren had possessed in centuries.","Spanning several high mesas linked by suspended rope bridges, Thunder Bluff seamlessly blends natural architecture with tauren practicality. The central bluffs host the bustling markets, bank, inn, and towering Wind Rider roost, while three specialized mesas branch out across the abyss. Hunter Rise serves the city's scouts and trackers; Elder Rise hosts lorekeepers and the Cenarion Circle under Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem; and Spirit Rise is devoted to spiritual communion, sheltering shamans, priests, and the mysterious subterranean caverns known as the Pools of Vision."],"hash":"f8b36f","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"1efba7d2b3","sec":93},"female-narrator":{"sha":"f9c02b9117","sec":100}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Thunder Bluff","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thunder_Bluff"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/cairne-bloodhoof","n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/zone/mulgore","n":"Mulgore","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/magatha-grimtotem","n":"Magatha Grimtotem","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/pools-of-vision","n":"Pools of Vision","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/elder-rise","n":"Elder Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hunter-rise","n":"Hunter Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/spirit-rise","n":"Spirit Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/97957-camping-101-herbalism","n":"Camping 101: Herbalism","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/npc/clarice-foster","n":"Clarice Foster","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/item/galvanized-horn","n":"Galvanized Horn","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bloodhoof-village","n":"Bloodhoof Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/golden-plains","n":"Golden Plains","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/elder-rise","n":"Elder Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/high-rise","n":"High Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hunter-rise","n":"Hunter Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/pools-of-vision","n":"Pools of Vision","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/spirit-rise","n":"Spirit Rise","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/ahanu","n":"Ahanu","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/bashana-runetotem","n":"Bashana Runetotem","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/bluff-runner-windstrider","n":"Bluff Runner Windstrider","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/dendrite-starblaze","n":"Dendrite Starblaze","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/falla-sagewind","n":"Falla Sagewind","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/holt-thunderhorn","n":"Holt Thunderhorn","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/innkeeper-pala","n":"Innkeeper Pala","k":"npc"},{